<ontology/use_brewing_distilling/use_brewing_distilling__0239__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 610" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n610> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Malt used in Brewing, Malting & Distilling: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 610"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "MALT: (GER. Maly. DU. Mout. DA. and SW. Malt. FR. Mal, Blégermé. IT. Malto. SP. Cebada retonada ó entallecida. RUS. Solod. POL. Slod. LAT. Malum.) is, correctly, any corn prepared after a particular manner, for brewing the various kinds of beer; but in its general acceptance is applied only to barley so prepared.—Before we proceed to state the method of maki..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_brewing_distilling/use_brewing_distilling__0239__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 952" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n952> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Malt used in Brewing, Malting & Distilling: J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 952"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "MALT: (Ger. maly; Dutch, mout; Fr. mal, blégerme; Ital. malto; Span. cebada retonada ó entallecida; Russ. solod; Lat. maltum). The term malt is applied to designate grain which, being steeped in water, is made to germinate to a certain extent, after which the process is checked by the application of heat. This evolves the saccharine principle of the grain, w..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_brewing_distilling/use_brewing_distilling__0239__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. MALT" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Malt used in Brewing, Malting & Distilling: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. MALT"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "MALT: (Eng. and Fr.; Malz, Germ.) is barley-corn, which has been subjected to an artificial process of germination. See BEER. Table of the Quantity of Malt consumed by the undermentioned Brewers of London and Vicinity, from October 10th, 1836, to October 10th, 1837."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

