<ontology/use_calico_printing/use_calico_printing__0557__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Alkali used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The goods must be washed within 24 hours after being printed. 10. Topical grounding blue for the cylinder press. Take 3-1/2 gallons of caustic soda lye of spec. grav. 1·15. 3-1/2 lbs. of ground indigo. 5 lbs. of precipitated protoxide of tin (as above)."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "essay_context" .

