<ontology/use_calico_printing/use_calico_printing__0562__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Rosin used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "At E and H are prolongations of the box, in which are set the vessels F G for holding the reserve paste. Preparation of the reserve or resist paste.--Melt in a kettle 2-1/2 libs. of rosin; 1 lib. of suet: mix well, and put it into the basins F G."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

