<ontology/use_calico_printing/use_calico_printing__doc_muriatic_acid__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. CHLORINE" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Muriatic Acid used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. CHLORINE"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "In the chloride of lime apparatus, most generally used by the skilful calico-printers of Mulhausen, the mixture of muriatic acid and manganese is put into glass globes, with long necks, heated upon a sand-bath."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

