<ontology/use_chocolate_confectionery/use_chocolate_confectionery__0118__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 361" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b31361584/page/n361/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cochineal used in Chocolate & Confectionery: Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 361"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Grades. USES AND COMMERCIAL FORMS OF COCHINEAL.—Cochineal was formerly much employed in dyeing wool, silk, and cotton: to-day it is a colour-ingredient of drugs and confectionery, and an artists' pigment."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

