<ontology/use_chocolate_confectionery/use_chocolate_confectionery__0138__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section CACAO OR COCOA" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/15191> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cocoa used in Chocolate & Confectionery: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section CACAO OR COCOA"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "CACAO: The chocolate nuts or seeds, termed cacao, are the fruit of species of Theobroma, an evergreen tree, native of the Western Continent. That commonly grown is T. cacao; but Lindley enumerates two other species, T. bicolor, a native of New Granada; and T. Guianensis, with yellow flowers, a native of Guiana. The seeds being nourishing and agreeable to mos..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_chocolate_confectionery/use_chocolate_confectionery__0138__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. CHLORINE" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cocoa used in Chocolate & Confectionery: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. CHLORINE"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The fatty matter is of the consistence of tallow, white, of a mild agreeable taste, called butter of cacao, and not apt to turn rancid by keeping."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_chocolate_confectionery/use_chocolate_confectionery__0138__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 372" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b31361584/page/n372/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cocoa used in Chocolate & Confectionery: Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 372"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Confectioners are said to find cocoanut butter an entirely satisfactory substitute for the more expensive cacao butter (see p. 1076), the imports of which into England have in consequence for some years past materially declined."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

