<ontology/use_chocolate_confectionery/use_chocolate_confectionery__0695__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 242" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n242/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Liquorice used in Chocolate & Confectionery: Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 242"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Liquorice is much used in the Levant in making a decoction which is drunk cold in summer, and liquorice water is a favourite beverage in this country with children. See GOONCH. LIQUORICE-JUICE, the inspissated juice of the liquorice root, boiled to a consistency for rolling into paste, and used for confectionery purposes."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

