<ontology/use_glass_ceramics/use_glass_ceramics__1202__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 362" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n362> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Zaffre used in Glassmaking, Pottery & Porcelain: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 362"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "SMALTS: a vitreous substance obtained by melting together zaffres, a regulus of cobalt, potash and siliceous matter, and grinding the produce to a fine powder, commercially known as powder-blue. It is employed to give a blue tinge to writing-paper, linen, and starch, and, not being affected by fire, is much employed in painting earthenware. Some is made in t..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_glass_ceramics/use_glass_ceramics__1202__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 1024" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n1024/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Zaffre used in Glassmaking, Pottery & Porcelain: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 1024"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Z E DZ I N ZAFFRE is the oxyde of cobalt, employed in painting pottery-ware and cobalt of a blue colour. See COBALT. ZE A, Indian Corn. The only species, the mays, or maize."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

