<ontology/use_metallurgy_tinplate/use_metallurgy_tinplate__0562__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. TABLE" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Rosin used in Metallurgy, Smelting, Brass & Tinplate: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. TABLE"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The best way of reducing the chloride of silver, says Mohr, is to mix it with one-third of its weight of colophony (black rosin), and to heat the mixture moderately in a crucible till the flame ceases to have a greenish-blue colour; then suddenly to increase the fire, so as to melt the metal into an ingot."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_metallurgy_tinplate/use_metallurgy_tinplate__0562__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 937" ;
