    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "SMALTS: a vitreous substance obtained by melting together zaffres, a regulus of cobalt, potash and siliceous matter, and grinding the produce to a fine powder, commercially known as powder-blue. It is employed to give a blue tinge to writing-paper, linen, and starch, and, not being affected by fire, is much employed in painting earthenware. Some is made in t..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

