    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "ESPARTO: a name given in Spain to the herbaceous stalks of the Machrochlea (Stipa tenacissima), a grass which is used for mats, sandals, cordage, and for paper pulp."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_paper_making/use_paper_making__0822__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 877" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b31361584/page/n877/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Esparto and other Vegetable Fibres for making Paper used in Paper Making & Cardboard: Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 877"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Moreover, as paper fibre, like esparto, must be fit for almost immediate immersion in the vats, paper-making can never pay the cost of separation and preparation, however simple and inexpensive."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_paper_making/use_paper_making__0822__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 1104" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n1104/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Esparto and other Vegetable Fibres for making Paper used in Paper Making & Cardboard: McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 1104"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "This led our paper makers to search diligently for good substitutes for rags, and their choice seems to have fallen chiefly on Esparto."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

