<ontology/use_perfumery_cosmetics/use_perfumery_cosmetics__1599__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 1064" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b31361584/page/n1064> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Benzoin used in Perfumery, Pomades & Essential Oils: Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 1064"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "STYRAX BENZOIN: The Benzoin Tree. The Resin = lubán (Ind. bazárs), hussí, shambiráni, kaminian, etc. A small tree of the Malay Archipelago, important as yielding the true Benzoin or Gum Benjamin of commerce. This substance appears to have been first mentioned by Ibn Batuta (Voy., etc., Fr. ed. 1858, iv., 228, 240), who visited Sumatra (A.D. 1325–49). He call..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_perfumery_cosmetics/use_perfumery_cosmetics__1599__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BENJAMIN" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Benzoin used in Perfumery, Pomades & Essential Oils: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BENJAMIN"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Benzoin is of great use in perfumery, as it enters into a number of preparations; among which may be mentioned fumigating pastilles, fumigating cloves (called also nails), poudre à la maréchale, &c."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_perfumery_cosmetics/use_perfumery_cosmetics__1599__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section MYROBALANS" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/15191> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Benzoin used in Perfumery, Pomades & Essential Oils: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section MYROBALANS"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "A milky juice is said to flow from T. angustifolia, which, when dried, is fragrant, and, resembling Benzoin, is used as a kind of incense in the Catholic churches in the Mauritius."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

