<ontology/use_perfumery_cosmetics/use_perfumery_cosmetics__doc_musk__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 651" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n651> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Musk used in Perfumery, Pomades & Essential Oils: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 651"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "MUSK-SEED: (GER. Bisamkörner. DU. Muskuszaad. DA. Desmerkorn. SW. Desmanskorn. FR. Ambrette, Grain musquée. IT. Granelli d'ambretta. SP. Ambarilla. PORT. Ambaralli. POL. Ziarka pigmowe. LAT. Abelmoschi grana,) is the seed of a plant which grows in Egypt, the West Indies, and in Gallam, a kingdom of Africa. This seed yields an odour precisely similar to that ..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_perfumery_cosmetics/use_perfumery_cosmetics__doc_musk__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 641" ;
