<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__0185__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. GUM" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Arabic used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. GUM"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Gum arabic is used in medicine, as also to give lustre to crapes and other silk stuffs. Gum senegal, is collected by the negroes during the month of November, from the acacia senegal, a tree 18 or 20 feet high."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__0185__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 28" ;
