<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__0750__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 27" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n27> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cream of Tartar used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 27"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "ARGOL: an acidulous concreto salt, the crust or sediment of wine vats and casks, which when purified is denominated cream of tartar; it is white or red, according to the wine of which it is the deposit, and largely used in medicine and the arts; also a Tartar name for the dried excrements of animals moulded into cakes and sold as fuel."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__0750__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 256" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n256> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cream of Tartar used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 256"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "CREAM OF TARTAR: (GER. Weinsteinrahm. DU. Wynsteenroom. DA. Wynsteenflöde. SW. Winstenflötor. FR. Crème de tartre. IT. Crema di tartaro. SP. Creemor tartaro. PORT. Creemor de tartaro. LAT. Creemor tartari,) called also crystals of tartar, is a preparation of tartar, and comes to us from Leghorn, and other parts of Italy. It is a combination of tartaric acid ..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__0750__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 116" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n116/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cream of Tartar used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 116"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Pure argol, or cream of tartar, is extensively used in medicine."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

