    rdfs:label "Evidence for Naphtha used in India-Rubber, Gutta-Percha & Waterproofing: Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 661"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "INDIA-RUBBERModern DemandSPECIAL CULTIVATION Three years later Mackintosh created the waterproofing trade by dissolving rubber in naphtha."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_rubber_waterproofing/use_rubber_waterproofing__1216__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 46" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n46/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Naphtha used in India-Rubber, Gutta-Percha & Waterproofing: Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 46"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "It is of a yellowish gold colour with occasionally white almond-like masses in it; there are, however, two or three varieties which enter into commerce. BENZOLE, an oil obtained from coal-naphtha, of great solvent powers, which is used by manufacturers of India-rubber and gutta-percha, by chemists for making oil of bitter almonds."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

