<ontology/use_soap_manufacture/use_soap_manufacture__1504__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. OILS" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Oil Seed used in Soap Manufacture: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. OILS"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "It is used extensively for making both soft soap and varnishes. Linseed oil, is obtained in greatest purity by cold pressure; but by a steam heat of about 200° F. a very good oil may be procured in larger quantity."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

