    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "TURPENTINE: Oil of, (GER. Terpentinöl. DU. Terpentynolie. DA. Terpentinolja. SW. Terpentinaljo. FR. Eau de raze, Huile de terebenthine, Huile d'étherée. IT. Acqua di rasa. SR. Aguarras. PORT. Aguarras. RUS. Skipidarnoe masslo. POL. Oley Terpentinowy,) is the essential oil drawn from turpentine by distillation: there are two sorts of this oil; the best red, a..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__0578__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. RESIN, KAURI" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Turpentine Oil used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. RESIN, KAURI"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "A solution in alcohol, mixed with one-fourth of its bulk of a solution in oil of turpentine, forms an excellent varnish, which dries quickly, is quite colourless, clear, and hard."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__0578__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 1117" ;
