    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Mastic used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 627"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "MASTICH: (GER. DA. and Sw. Mastix. DU. Mastik. FR. Mastic. IT. Mastice. SP. Almastica, Almacega. PORT. Almacega. RUS. Mastika. POL. Mastyks. LAT. Resina lentisina.) The lesser turpentine-tree, and the lentsicus, afford the mastic of commerce. See LENTISCK and GUM. It is used in fumigations, in the composition of varnishes, and is supposed to strengthen the g..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__1538__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. MASTIC" ;
