    rdfs:label "Evidence for Amber used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 977"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Gum-copal, and amber, are the substances principally employed in oil-varnishes; the copal being whitest, is used for varnishing light; the amber for dark colours."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

