<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__doc_sandarac__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1322" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n1322> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Sandarac used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 1322"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "SANDARACH: A resinous substance, commonly met with in loose granules a little larger than a pea, of a whitish yellow colour, brittle, inflammable, of a resinous smell, and acrid aromatic taste. It exudes, it is said, in warm climates, from cracks and incisions in the common juniper bush. It is used as a varnish, dissolved in spirits of wine, and the powder i..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__doc_sandarac__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. FULMINATES" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Sandarac used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. FULMINATES"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "An alcoholic solution of sandarach, commonly called spirit varnish, acts powerfully on copper, with the production of a green efflorescence, which decomposes fulminate of mercury."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__doc_sandarac__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 978" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n978/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Sandarac used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 978"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "If the varnish is to produce a red colour, more of the lac, and less of the sandarach should be used, and a little dragon's blood should be added."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .

